 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-004\",\n \"clauses\": {\"organize_data\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"Count the pictures in each row of the {pg_word}, then write the counts for {cat_list} in the {table_word}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F05 asks the learner to count the pictures in each row of the pictograph and write the counts into the table, which is organizing the pictograph's data into a table. The producing family is itself failing (see below), but the clause is producible.\"},\n \"pictograph\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Look at the {pg_word}. Write the correct count for each row in the {table_word}: {cat_list}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 names the pictograph as the object the learner reads (pg_word draws only on F01, which prints the gated word pictograph). The producing family is itself failing (see below), but the clause is producible.\"},\n \"without_scale\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F02\", \"template\": \"Each picture stands for 1 item.\", \"reasoning\": \"F02 is a hint stating a one-picture-to-one-item correspondence, which is the no-scale condition; the declared variant scale_type no_scale covers it. No family prints the word scale, which is NOT_YET_KNOWN.\"},\n \"table\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"The {pg_word} shows {cat_list}. Fill in the {table_word} with the correct counts.\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 asks the learner to fill in the table with counts. table_word prints only the gated word table, which is introduced for this lc. The producing family is itself failing (see below), but the clause is producible.\"}},\n \"failing_families\": [\"F05\", \"F06\", \"F07\", \"F09\"],\n \"failing_templates\": [\"Count the pictures in each row of the {pg_word}, then write the counts for {cat_list} in the {table_word}.\", \"Look at the {pg_word}. Write the correct count for each row in the {table_word}: {cat_list}.\", \"The {pg_word} shows {cat_list}. Fill in the {table_word} with the correct counts.\", \"{join} and {v}\"],\n \"overall\": \"FAIL\",\n \"reasoning\": \"Two defects. (1) Length: sentence_max_words is 15. F05 is a single sentence whose fixed wording alone is 14 words before cat_list (which adds at least 4 words) and 3 more after it, so every render exceeds 15 words. F06's second sentence is 10 fixed words plus the cat_list tokens; with two-word category members (Grade 1 through Grade 4 are in the F09 domain) it reaches 19 words. (2) Duplicates: F09 is '{join} and {v}', where join is F10 (three distinct members, distinct_in_every_render true) and v is drawn from the same category domain with no distinctness statement. Nothing in the domains stops v from equalling one of the three joined categories, so a learner can be shown one category twice in the list that the table must count, which is misleading. F06 and F07 print cat_list from F09 and inherit this fault. F02 (1 item per picture), F03, F04, F01 and F08 pass: they print only the gated word table or pictograph, or a count-based hint. F04's words (category, items, record) are common words not in NOT_YET_KNOWN, so they are not flagged.\"}",
